WEBVTT

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:05.170
Ta-dah!

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:13.410
"Pepper"

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.000
Greetings, all. It's the man you've been waiting for, Tsutomu Domon.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.700
Today, I think I will try chopping this onion.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.710
Sorry, could you...

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.440
Sure. Have a good day.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.510
Are you going to Nesta again?

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.610
If I do, that's my business.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.530
I can't remember them at all!

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.200
Focus. You need to at least learn your kanji properly.

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:50.310
"Tsutomu Domon

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:50.310
Entertainment On Stage Vol. 73"

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.700
Or you'll grow up to be like him.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.040
Yeah, I'll study my butt off.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.240
Tsutomu, have a tissue.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.440
I don't need to grow up just yet.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.280
Karan.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.550
That line was super very bad.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:56.420
Super very... what?

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.450
Super very bad? No one says that anymore!

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.960
--You banana be kidding me!
--That's old, too!

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.720
What is this?

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.960
"Mysterious Tree

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.960
A natural phenomenon?!"

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:07.960
"Asagaya West, 4-chome"

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.090
Can you see this mysterious sight?

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:07.100
Let me see.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.100
Oh, sure.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.930
According to the homeowner, it just happened at some point.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.970
"Mysterious Tree

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.970
A natural phenomenon?!"

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:14.970
"Asagaya West, 4-chome"

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.470
Is it possible for this to be done artificially?

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.960
Maki!

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:18.570
Big Brother, look at this!

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:19.910
Hold on!

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.740
--What is it?
--Wh-What?

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:23.450
Is it someone funnier than me?

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.980
No! Look closely at this.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:31.350
"Mysterious Tree

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:31.350
A natural phenomenon?!"

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:31.350
"Asagaya West, 4-chome"

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.820
Why is there an M.J.B.K.?

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:31.320
What? An M.J.B.K.? Where?

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.090
You can't see it?

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.090
Huh? Where is it?

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:36.490
Right here!

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.760
Come on, that's my phone...

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.600
It was like this when you woke up?

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.500
"Mysterious Tree

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.500
A natural phenomenon?!"

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.500
"Asagaya West, 4-chome"

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.470
It was a peach tree, a pepper tree, and a surprise for me.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.600
Regular people can't see it.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.170
Wait, isn't that one supposed to be dead?

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:51.770
My phone!

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:54.010
"Death"

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.850
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:04.350
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:13.560
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin',</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:19.570
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief" look very similar</i>

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:24.970
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:30.750
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:37.090
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.990
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.920
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:47.830
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:53.270
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin',</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:59.340
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:04.780
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin',</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.790
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.720
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.460
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.390
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:22.230
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:29.640
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.470
"Ah! Days of Our Youth"

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.710
It looks like you're busy again today.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:42.750
It'll be easy, easy, easy-peasy.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.220
The currently unfolding situation

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:49.120
where sayings that had fallen out of use and dead words run rampant

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:52.120
has been determined to be caused by the M.J.B.K.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.430
We did it, baby!

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:55.400
We're putting our backs into it!

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.230
We are!

00:03:56.230 --> 00:03:57.430
Oh, gosh, where are you looking?

00:03:57.430 --> 00:04:00.730
Letch, sketch, one touch.

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:06.110
Truly, this is the afterlife of dead words.

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.470
"The afterlife of dead words

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.470
that everyone knows."

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.480
We sent out the Vectors for recon,

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:11.980
and the kanji for "death" was the one acting strangely.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:14.280
However...

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:17.250
There's... no M.J.B.K.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.260
This is likely a special characteristic of the kanji for death.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:23.290
Death does not have life.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:26.130
So the M.J.B.K. for death doesn't exist.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.800
Instead, the concept of death itself is wavering,

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:31.960
and other M.J.B.K.s have revived.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.100
But why are they in our world?

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.810
Does that work?

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.510
Due to the large-scale battle with the nothingness M.J.B.K.,

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:44.780
the Logos World is highly unstable at the moment.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:47.120
Like what happened the other day.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.350
Probably, like when Hito appeared in our world,

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:55.160
this is due to the boundary between the Logos World and ours thinning.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.030
The M.J.B.K.s that have appeared are weak,

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:01.800
and ordinary people with weak
Verbalism Ability can't see them,

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.030
so right now, it's not causing too much chaos.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:08.340
However, given the existence of a death M.J.B.K.,

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:12.370
to end this chaos, we need to subdue the revived M.J.B.K.s.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.370
Question!

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:16.980
Subdue them? Are M.J.B.K.s something we can beat by ourselves?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:17.880
Not a chance.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:21.050
The only thing that can defeat an M.J.B.K. is an Aquarion.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.150
Then what do we do?

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:27.690
Aquarion isn't supposed to be able to Gattai in our world.

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:31.690
So, can we throw up our hands in despair and go take a nap?

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.730
Like, come on, guys!

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.030
How lazy are you?

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:42.370
I have a plan. If we can't beat them in our world...

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.540
...we'll just send them back to M.J.B.K. space.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.580
Is that possible?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.010
Yes.

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:53.880
And so, in response to the appearance of M.J.B.K.s in our world,

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.720
I have decided to form a special task force!

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.920
Its name is... the Asagaya Yurei Busters!

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.090
♪ Yurei Busters! ♪

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.360
--The Asagaya Yurei Busters?!
--♪ Yurei Busters! ♪

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.200
You are the team members.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:15.070
Uh, can't we just be the Verbalism Club?

00:06:15.070 --> 00:06:17.710
Why does this chorus make me feel so uneasy?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:21.580
I thought this might happen, so the uniforms are already made.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:22.910
Get changed.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.050
Why jumpsuits?

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.080
No clue.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:28.050
They aren't cute.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.050
We are the Yurei Busters!

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.990
I like that piece of equipment.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:36.060
Head out, Asagaya Yurei Busters!

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:38.260
To protect the future of Asagaya!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:40.400
You're so into this that it's off-putting.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:43.100
The manager seems to have cheered back up.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.790
She's forcing herself to.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.900
"Asagaya

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:48.900
Meiwa Bakery"

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:48.900
As full of surprises as a treasure chest!

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:53.570
This roll pan is just too twisted!

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.240
You seem troubled.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.410
Who're you?

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.810
We are the task force to save the word.

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.840
The Asagaya Yurei Busters!

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:07.490
I've got a reading.

00:07:07.490 --> 00:07:09.090
Is it over there?

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:11.490
What did I do?

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.260
--Found it!
--The time for judgment is upon us.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:20.170
Aquaripen!

00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:23.600
It's an experimental piece of equipment developed by Deava--the Aquaripen.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:28.610
"All-purpose Pen-shaped M.J.B.K.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:28.610
Fighting Stationary [Aquaripen]"

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:28.610
With this, you can use Verbalism to some degree in the real world. Probably.

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.510
Go straight, direct!

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:34.980
"Direct"

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.450
Maki!

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.950
Whoa, it really disappeared!

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:39.120
By manifesting an appropriate word,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.120
it's possible to damage an M.J.B.K.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.690
That should have sent it to the death dimension.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:47.860
Maia, you were c-cool.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:50.330
We have defeated thirteen M.J.B.K.s.

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:52.000
Only twelve left to go now, huh?

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.700
The M.J.B.K.s have all gathered in Asagaya, I see.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.500
Why is that, anyway?

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:58.010
I can't say with any certainty.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:02.310
Many great writers are said to have come from Asagaya.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:06.510
Perhaps, even in death, the souls of those literary giants

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:09.150
are drawing the M.J.B.K.s here.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.490
I don't care.

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.690
Let's fix all this weird nostalgia.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:15.990
They aren't fond memories to look back on for me.

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:19.160
I don't get anything they're saying, so it's boring!

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.830
No way. No way. He's not my boyfriend, he's just my wheels, you know?

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:25.830
I want a guy to be my meal ticket, too!

00:08:25.830 --> 00:08:29.200
Fix this nostalgia? You're sure they said that?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:32.170
Yeah, man! That's totally what they said!

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:33.410
Wait!

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.540
--Mushi! Mushi!
--Natsu!

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.680
Mushi. Mushi. Mushishi.

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.200
Hold on.

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:42.350
Ah! The M.J.B.K.!

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:46.520
We won't let things go your way!

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.360
No, we won't!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.690
Who are you people?

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.700
I don't know what you're doing.

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:58.270
But if doing away with this cool vibe we've got going on is your goal...

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.440
...I can't let you do that.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.270
Because we're...

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:04.940
...shining our brightest, baby!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.380
We're so happening!

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.880
What is this?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.880
You're way past the age for this. It's creepy.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:12.450
Man, this is painful to watch.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:16.220
What was that, punk?
I'll throw <i>nata de coco</i> at you!

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:17.550
I see.

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.290
Along with the rush of outdated expressions,

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.590
they've gone back to feeling how they did as youths, huh?

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.060
This is awkward.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.890
What's with that soy sauce face?

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.760
Don't get carried away just because we're trendy.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:32.070
Respecting your elders should be as obvious as an Atari Maeda Cracker.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.100
What are they even saying?

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:36.900
What's with these horribly lame people?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.410
They're MK5s.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:40.140
Huh? What's that mean?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.140
It means she's ready to Murder or Kill them in about five seconds.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.940
We've got one here, too.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.610
What?

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:50.280
The word corrosion rate is rising!

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.650
Something is here.

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:59.160
What's my dead grandpa doing here?

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.430
Dad! You died in an accident three years ago!

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:05.500
This is whack!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:09.000
"Death"

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.100
This is...

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:12.500
Death... is trying to change the world.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.790
It looks like the dead kanji in M.J.B.K. space

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.520
are being destroyed over time.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:36.460
As that happens, the word corrosion rate keeps rising!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:39.730
There are signs of it appearing everywhere.

00:10:44.670 --> 00:10:46.300
Mom...

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:49.970
Wh-Why...

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.140
...are you here?

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.820
--Are you okay?
--My leg!!
--This is seriously bad news.

00:11:01.820 --> 00:11:05.160
--Ambulance! Ambulance!
--The living are being held back by the dead.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.830
This is super very bad.

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.530
Manager, you're too noisy.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:11.000
Shoko, that's mean!

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.700
Mushi. Mushi. Mushishi.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:15.170
"Wind"

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:16.370
Wind...

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:17.370
Next.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:19.010
There's no end to this!

00:11:19.010 --> 00:11:21.210
And this is...

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:24.380
They just keep increasing in number.

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:28.520
At this rate, the boundary between life and death will become vague.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.050
The world will be full of dead people.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:32.550
Living people will wander into the world of the dead.

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:35.390
It'll be awful!

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:37.220
Let's go. We'll end this quickly.

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:41.090
Yeah, it's time for the Yurei Busters to act.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:51.370
"Kanji Dictionaries"

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.530
Kento? What are you doing?

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:51.870
If we deal with the M.J.B.K.s one by one, it will take forever.

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:57.040
I'll see if I can find a kanji that will let us affect the death M.J.B.K. directly.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:00.880
Normally, we have to rely on the kids' Verbalism Ability and Aquarion.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.710
This time, I can do something!

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.580
You have a point. I'll help, too.

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.560
What was that?

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:14.560
Yume. Yume.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:16.060
What is that?!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:18.570
Yume? Yu...

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:22.140
--Why? Why is it so big?
--What is going on?

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.640
--This makes no sense.
--U-Um...

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:25.310
--Okay, gather round!
--Um...

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.310
Attention here, please.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:31.750
You are not rotten apples.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:36.420
It's never too late to start!

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.590
Dreams come true!

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:40.920
Never give up on your dreams!

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:43.080
I'll work hard for my dreams.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:47.430
I-I'll try to erase it.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.760
No, I'd say that's not gonna happen.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:53.170
You don't know until you try, right, Big Brother?

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:54.660
I see.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.810
Their hearts have been ensnared by dreams,

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:02.280
and that's having an effect on the M.J.B.K., huh?

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.150
Then there's only one solution...

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.450
Wh-What's up, Hayato?

00:13:06.450 --> 00:13:07.850
B-Big Brother?

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:12.150
Yes, dreams will make you a bigger person!

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:15.960
You guys... You guys...

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:20.120
I believed you would understand!

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.800
Stop this at once.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.370
Your dreams will never come true.

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.640
What are you saying, you dunce?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.300
If you don't give up on your dreams, they come true!

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.710
Let me ask, then.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:33.710
Wh-What?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:37.140
How many of you played baseball as children?

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:44.820
And how many of you dreamed of playing professionally?

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.880
Did that dream come true?

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:57.000
It's a delusion to think your dreams will come true if you just believe.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.730
It's not because people give up that their dreams don't come true.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:03.540
It's because their dreams don't come true that they give up.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:06.910
Hard work alone doesn't mean you can do anything.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:09.540
Do you think the greatest pitcher in the world

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:13.850
is the one who's put in the most hard work?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:15.550
Obviously not!

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:18.190
Every person has their own special traits.

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:22.060
Where you can and can't go is delineated by talent.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:23.860
Yet you...

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:28.060
You say their dreams will surely come true if they work hard.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:32.270
That mistaken teaching gives people false hope.

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.270
It ultimately brings them misfortune.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:37.370
Listen, most dreams never come true.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:40.610
Your misplaced work goes to waste more often than not.

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:44.080
And chasing after dreams, now, at your ages?

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:47.250
It would be insane to think you'll see any results.

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.720
Do any of you have families?

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.790
A wife? Children?

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:55.460
If you do, stop wasting your time here on impossible dreams,

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.730
and take good care of those closest to you!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:01.100
And teach your children this...

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:04.270
"You were born to a plain, ordinary guy like me,

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:07.640
so I'm sure you don't have the talent to be someone great!

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:12.400
But live your hardest, anyway!"

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.310
Did you have to go that far?

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.810
Now, do it.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:19.910
Huh?

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:22.750
Don't "huh?" at me. The M.J.B.K. is weakened!

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:27.310
--Ah!
--P-People's dreams are f-fleeting.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:30.090
"Fleeting"

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:32.360
Yume...

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:37.090
W-We did it. B-But...

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:40.470
Big Brother, you fiend.

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:41.600
Fiendman.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:43.300
You're the devil!

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:45.110
I'll cry, too.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.440
That way! I saw one!

00:15:47.440 --> 00:15:48.930
Crap!

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:53.780
Hold it! I'm not letting you get away!

00:15:53.780 --> 00:15:54.620
You're...

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:58.280
You're not getting past us.
How do you like that miso?

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:04.450
You people... Do you even understand what's happening?

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:08.460
If the boundary between life and death vanishes,

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.460
there will be serious damage done.

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.530
This is a threat to the world.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:15.300
If you intend to promote it,

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:17.810
I won't show any mercy.

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:19.810
Akira.

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:23.140
Huh? What're you getting all serious for?

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.810
That's not in style, you know.

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.980
Wh-What?

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.550
What's wrong with what we're doing?

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.820
We've found the passion we lost!

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:34.320
It's like we're young again!

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:37.880
Is having fun wrong? What's wrong with it?!

00:16:44.830 --> 00:16:47.330
Master... Sougon...

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.500
Wait, you!

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:52.510
Lost sight of it...

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:54.340
Oh, Hayato, what's up?

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.870
Go on ahead without me.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:00.500
Dad...

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.590
Hito...

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:09.590
Everyone is happy. What's wrong with this?

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.860
Answer me!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.850
Step aside.

00:17:14.030 --> 00:17:15.860
Those kids can't get through.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:17.920
Kids?

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:23.100
"Halloween Party in Asagaya

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:23.100
Pearl Shopping Street"

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.370
The M.J.B.K. sh-should be around here.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:31.050
What a racket!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.210
Yeah.

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:33.610
What is that?

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:35.880
P-Para Para?

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.550
We can't get in.

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:40.120
I want to play.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.760
Those kids...

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:44.220
Ugh! I'm mad!

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:47.730
Do you know why words die out?

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:51.900
There are times in their lives when people shine brightest.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:55.630
Those become text in the form of trendy words.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:00.270
What? What happened?

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:01.940
Who stopped the music?

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:04.410
Cut it out already!

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:10.980
But you can't monopolize the time to shine for yourselves.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:16.990
We don't even have memories to be nostalgic about yet!

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:18.260
Get out of our way!

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:20.990
That's our place!

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:25.470
I want to become an adult, too!

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:28.770
You have to cede the road to the future.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:30.600
That's why death exists.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:33.270
For words and for people.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.680
Don't come back now.

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:39.110
I'm already standing on my own two feet.

00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:46.950
Though I'm struggling with the lack of talent I inherited from you.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:52.790
You good now?

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:56.530
Yeah. I'll be fine.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:59.170
You came because you were worried.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:02.230
Sorry to be such a high-maintenance old lady.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.560
I'll have to make a grave for you.

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:11.480
I've found it! This one will work!

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:13.680
I've just sent you the map.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:16.150
All members of the Asagaya Yurei Busters

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:18.220
are to gather at the designated spot on the map at once!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.720
And all of you materialize kanji there together.

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:25.590
Huh? I can't write this kanji!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.330
"Kanji Drills"

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.730
Here.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:31.670
You want to be an adult, right?

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:37.830
"Mimi Pharmacy"

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:44.740
Trick or treat!

00:19:48.050 --> 00:19:51.020
Here. Wear this.

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:55.590
It looks good on you. Have fun.

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:57.520
Thank you!

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:00.620
Maia, I will save the world.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.370
Yeah, I know!

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:12.210
I am the savior who will save everything!

00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:14.710
If you're lonely,

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.570
I'll be at your side and save you anytime.

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:24.720
Is everyone ready?

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.720
I'm good to go anytime.

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:27.890
Y-Yes!

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:29.460
I-I'm fine.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:30.890
Now, let's do it!

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:32.890
Yeah, let's do this!

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:35.130
Dead words and drifting souls,

00:20:35.130 --> 00:20:37.900
rest in peace beneath the grass and trees!

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:39.630
Burial!

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:43.970
"Burial"

00:20:55.580 --> 00:20:57.350
Goodbye.

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.990
Huh? Why am I dressed like this? It's cold!

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:07.590
Why Bodycon fashion? Yuck!

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:11.100
--Well, back to work again tomorrow.
--Let's work hard.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:16.330
Now we just have to eliminate the little M.J.B.K. sent to the other side.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:34.510
Project.

00:21:36.120 --> 00:21:38.360
Why did the monitor turn on by itself?

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:41.500
The M.J.B.K.s have gone back to their original giant forms?

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.200
Stay there and watch.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.690
Who is it?

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:49.130
O pitiful souls of the departed.

00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:52.800
Let all of you be reduced...

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.310
...to light.

00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:04.990
With one strike...

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:07.050
N-No way...!

00:22:19.670 --> 00:22:21.160
Akira...

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:52.960
What is an excavation, maki?

00:23:52.960 --> 00:23:55.260
It's digging up old stuff, yume.

00:23:55.260 --> 00:23:56.430
Genohoika!

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:58.930
No, mushi. The dig site is...

00:23:58.930 --> 00:24:00.270
In a foreign desert, uzu.

00:24:00.270 --> 00:24:01.270
It's hot, honoo.

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:02.940
They don't speak Japanese there, natsu.

00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:05.510
--Maki!
--You can't watch <i>Logos</i> there, yume.

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:06.770
Episode 16.

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:09.510
"Episode 16: Carve Them In!

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:09.510
The Scars of Destiny"

00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:09.840
"Carve Them In! The Scars of Destiny."

00:24:09.840 --> 00:24:10.830
I'm scared.
